There are no symptoms. Signs vary but may include bradycardia; an LV impulse that is laterally displaced,

enlarged, and increased in amplitude; a systolic ejection (flow) murmur at the left lower sternal border; a

3rd heart sound (S

) due to early, rapid diastolic ventricular filling; a 4th heart sound (S

), heard best

during resting bradycardia because diastolic filling time is increased; and hyperdynamic carotid pulses.
